18:T70a,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","inLanguage":"en","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Studomate replace TIA Portal, Automgen or CODESYS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, and that is not its purpose. Studomate is for learning and practice: it simulates GRAFCET, ladder logic and HMI pages in the browser. It does not program an industrial PLC (Siemens, Schneider…), though it can drive an Arduino board. In class it complements the software of the workshop's PLC: students design and test their logic in Studomate, in the lab or at home, then carry it over to the real hardware. The notations follow the standards: IEC 60848 for GRAFCET, IEC 61131-3 blocks (TON, TOF, CTU…) for ladder logic."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can students practise at home without PLC software?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Studomate is free and runs in the browser with no installation, on Windows, macOS or Linux. A student can redo a lab exercise or follow the course on their own computer, with no licence and no hardware."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does anything need to be installed on the lab computers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. A recent browser is enough. Only using an Arduino board requires Chrome or Edge."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do students need to create an account?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Without an account, they open the shared project and work in their browser. An account, with or without an email address, lets them find their projects on another device and share their own by link."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Studomate free to use in class?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, in class as at home. The code is free software under the AGPL v3 licence."}}]}7:["$","$L17",null,{"maxWidth":"md","sx":{"my":4},"children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$18"}}],["$","$L19",null,{"variant":"h2","component":"h1","color":"primary","gutterBottom":true,"children":"Teaching GRAFCET and ladder logic with Studomate"}],["$","$L19",null,{"fontSize":"1.1rem","children":"Studomate is a free GRAFCET, ladder logic and HMI simulator that runs in the browser. It is used to prepare, hand out and mark automation lab exercises, in vocational and technical programmes (BTS CRSA, BTS ATI, BTS Électrotechnique, bac pro MELEC, STI2D, BUT GEII) and in engineering schools."}],["$","$L1a",null,{"sx":{"my":2}}],[["$","$L1b","Preparing a lab exercise",{"component":"section","children":[["$","$L19",null,{"variant":"h3","component":"h2","gutterBottom":true,"mt":5,"children":"Preparing a lab exercise"}],["$","$L1b",null,{"component":"ul","sx":{"pl":3,"my":0},"children":[["$","$L19","0",{"component":"li","mb":1,"children":"Start from a ready-made project: traffic light, crossroads, car park barrier, elevator, drilling or carton sorting. Each comes in an exercise version and a solution version."}],["$","$L19","1",{"component":"li","mb":1,"children":"Write the exercise statement in Markdown in the project properties: it travels with the project and opens in a tab."}],["$","$L19","2",{"component":"li","mb":1,"children":"Keep the solution in a separate project that you do not share."}]]}]]}],["$","$L1b","Handing the project out to students",{"component":"section","children":[["$","$L19",null,{"variant":"h3","component":"h2","gutterBottom":true,"mt":5,"children":"Handing the project out to students"}],["$","$L1b",null,{"component":"ul","sx":{"pl":3,"my":0},"children":[["$","$L19","0",{"component":"li","mb":1,"children":"From your account, share a link: each student who opens it gets their own copy, without creating an account. The link can be revoked at any time."}],"$L1c"]}]]}],"$L1d","$L1e","$L1f"],"$L20","$L21","$L22"]}]
